cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "EE10 — Electrical Engineering Research Project: Course Syllabus and Materials"
message: "If you refer to these course materials, please cite them as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Guido"
    given-names: "Ryan Manuel D."
    affiliation: "Rizal Technological University, Cities of Mandaluyong and Pasig, Philippines"
abstract: >-
  A fifteen-week outcomes-based course design for an undergraduate electrical
  engineering research project. The course runs two linked studies back to back:
  Phase 1 produces a research project proposal and a review or scientometric
  paper submitted to an IEEE venue indexed in IEEE Xplore; Phase 2 executes,
  calibrates, and validates a working prototype and reports it as a full IEEE
  article defended before a panel. Includes the syllabus, twelve companion unit
  lecture pages, and eleven course templates.
keywords:
  - engineering education
  - research methods
  - scientometrics
  - bibliometrics
  - capstone design
  - electrical engineering
  - IEEE Xplore
  - design thinking
